# Files that run or are parsed on Linux and macOS are LF in every checkout,
# including a Windows one with core.autocrlf: a CR after a shebang makes the
# kernel look for `bash\r`, and dpkg, systemd and launchd read these files as
# they are. The packaging tests check them byte for byte on every OS.
*.sh                      text eol=lf
agent/packaging/linux/**  text eol=lf
agent/packaging/darwin/** text eol=lf
